{
  "title": "13: al-Ra'd الرعد",
  "code": "012",
  "data": "بِسْمِ اللهِ الرَّحْمٰنِ الرَّحِيْمِ\nBISMIL LAAHIR RAHMAANIR RAHEEM\nIn the Name of Allah, the All-beneficent, the All-merciful\nالٓمّٓرٰ تِلْكَ اٰيٰتُ الْكِتٰبِؕ وَالَّذِىْۤ اُنْزِلَ اِلَيْكَ مِنْ رَّبِّكَ الْحَقُّ وَلٰكِنَّ اَكْثَرَ النَّاسِ لَا يُؤْمِنُوْنَ‏(1)\nALAAMMAARAA TILKA AAYAATUL AL-KETAABE WAL LAZEE UNZELA ELAYKA MIN RABBEKA HAQQO LAAKINNAL AKSARAN NAASE LAA YOAMENOONA.\nAlif, Lam, Mim, Ra (A. L. M. R.), These are the verses of the Book, and that which hath been sent down unto thee from thy Lord is the Truth, but most people believe it not.\nاَللّٰهُ الَّذِىْ رَفَعَ السَّمٰوٰتِ بِغَيْرِ عَمَدٍ تَرَوْنَهَا ثُمَّ اسْتَوٰى عَلَى الْعَرْشِ وَسَخَّرَ الشَّمْسَ وَالْقَمَرَؕ كُلٌّ يَّجْرِىْ لِاَجَلٍ مُّسَمًّىؕ يُدَبِّرُ الْاَمْرَ يُفَصِّلُ الْاٰيٰتِ لَعَلَّكُمْ بِلِقَآءِ رَبِّكُمْ تُوْقِنُوْنَ‏(2)\nALLAAHO LAZEE RAFAA’A SAMAAWAATE BEGHAYRIL A’MADIM TARAWNAHAA SUMMA TAWAA A’LAL A’RSHIL SAKHKHARASH SHAMSA WAL QAMARA KULLUL YYAJREAA LE-ELAA MOSAMMAA YUDABBERU AMRA YUFASSELU AAYAATE LA-A’LLAKUM BELEQAAE RABBEKUM TOOQENOONA.\nGod, it is Who raised the heavens without any pillars that ye see, then firmly established Himself on the Throne (of Absolute authority), and made subservient the sun and the moon (to His Will); each one to run its course to a time appointed (for it); Regulateth He the affair, explaineth He the signs (in detail) so that about the meeting with your Lord ye may be certain.\nوَهُوَ الَّذِىْ مَدَّ الْاَرْضَ وَجَعَلَ فِيْهَا رَوَاسِىَ وَاَنْهٰرًا ؕ وَمِنْ كُلِّ الثَّمَرٰتِ جَعَلَ فِيْهَا زَوْجَيْنِ اثْنَيْنِ يُغْشِى الَّيْلَ النَّهَارَ ؕ اِنَّ فِىْ ذٰ لِكَ لَاٰيٰتٍ لِّقَوْمٍ يَّتَفَكَّرُوْنَ‏(3)\nWA HOWA LAZEE MADDA ARZA WA FEEHAA JA-A’LA WA KHELAALAHAA WA MIN KULLE SAMARAATE JA-A’LA FEEHAA ZAWJAYNE NAYNE YUGHSHEAA LAYLA NAHAARA INNAL FEE ZAA LEKA LA-AAYAATIL LEQAWMINY YATAFAKKAROON.\nAnd He it is who spread out the earth and made in it firm mountains and (the flowing) rivers; and of all fruits He hath made in it pairs two (male and female) kinds; He causeth the night to enshroud the day; Verily in this there are signs for a people who reflect.\nوَ فِى الْاَرْضِ قِطَعٌ مُّتَجٰوِرٰتٌ وَّجَنّٰتٌ مِّنْ اَعْنَابٍ وَّزَرْعٌ وَّنَخِيْلٌ صِنْوَانٌ وَّغَيْرُ صِنْوَانٍ يُّسْقٰى بِمَآءٍ وَّاحِدٍ وَنُفَضِّلُ بَعْضَهَا عَلٰى بَعْضٍ فِى الْاُكُلِؕ اِنَّ فِىْ ذٰ لِكَ لَاٰيٰتٍ لِّقَوْمٍ يَّعْقِلُوْنَ‏(4)\nWA FIL ARZE QETAA’UN MMUTAJAAWERAATUN WWAJANNAATUN MIN AAA’NAABIN WWAZARA’UN WWANAKHEELUN SENWAANUN WWAGHAYRU SENWAANIN YYUSQAA BE-MAAA-IM WAAHEDIN WANUFAZZELU BAA’ZAHAA A’LAA ELAA FIL AL-AUKULE INNAL FEE ZAA LEKA LA-AAYAATIL LEQAWMINY YA’QELOON.\nAnd in the earth are tracts, side by side, and gardens of vine, and corn fields, and palm trees having one root and (others) having many (although) they are (all ) watered with water one (and the same); And yet some We make more excellent than others in fruits; Verily in this there are signs for people who understand.\nوَ اِنْ تَعْجَبْ فَعَجَبٌ قَوْلُهُمْ ءَاِذَا كُنَّا تُرٰبًا ءَاِنَّا لَفِىْ خَلْقٍ جَدِيْدٍ  ؕ اُولٰۤئِكَ الَّذِيْنَ كَفَرُوْا بِرَبِّهِمْۚ وَاُولٰۤئِكَ الْاَغْلٰلُ فِىْۤ اَعْنَاقِهِمْۚ وَاُولٰۤئِكَ اَصْحٰبُ النَّارِۚ هُمْ فِيْهَا خٰلِدُوْنَ‏(5)\nWA IN TAA’JAB FAA’AJABUN QAWLOHUM A-EZAA KUNNAA TORAABAWN A-INNAA LAFEE KHALQIN JADEEDIN AOOLAAEKA LAZEENA KAFAROO BE-RABBEHIM WAAWLAAEKA AL-AAGHLAALU FEE AAA’NAAQEHEM WAAWLAAEKA ASHAABUN NAAR HUM FEEHAA KHAALEDOON.\nAnd if thou wouldst wonder, then wondrous is their saying; “What! when we are dust would we then surely be (returned) in a new creation?” These are they who disbelieve in their Lord; and these shall have collars (of servitude) in their necks; And they are the companions of the (Hell) Fire; In it shall they abide.\nوَيَسْتَعْجِلُوْنَكَ بِالسَّيِّئَةِ قَبْلَ الْحَسَنَةِ وَقَدْ خَلَتْ مِنْ قَبْلِهِمُ الْمَثُلٰتُؕ وَاِنَّ رَبَّكَ لَذُوْ مَغْفِرَةٍ لِّلنَّاسِ عَلٰى ظُلْمِهِمْۚ وَاِنَّ رَبَّكَ لَشَدِيْدُ الْعِقَابِ‏(6)\nWA YASTA’JELOONAKA BIS-SAYYEATE QABLA HASANATE WA QAD KHALAT MIN QABLEHEMU AL-MASULAATU WA INNA RABBAKA LAZOO MAGHFERATIN LIN-NAASE A’LAA ZULMEHEM WA INNA RABBAKA LASHADEEDU E’QAAB.\nAnd they ask thou to hasten on the evil (the chastisement) before the good, and (although) indeed hath come to pass before them exemplary punishments; And verily thy Lord is indeed the Lord of forgiveness unto people despite their injustice; and verily thy Lord is severe in requital.\nوَيَقُوْلُ الَّذِيْنَ كَفَرُوْا لَوْلَاۤ اُنْزِلَ عَلَيْهِ اٰيَةٌ مِّنْ رَّبِّهٖؕ اِنَّمَاۤ اَنْتَ مُنْذِرٌ وَّ لِكُلِّ قَوْمٍ هَادٍ‏(7)\nWA YAQOOLO LAZEENA KAFAROO LAWLAA UNZELA A’LAYHE TAA-TEENAA MIN RABBEH INNAMAA ANTA MUNZERUN WA LEKULLIM QAWMIN HAADIN.\nAnd say those who disbelieve: “Why hath not a sign been sent down unto him (Muhammad) from his Lord?” Verily thou art a Warner and a guide unto every people.\nاَللّٰهُ يَعْلَمُ مَا تَحْمِلُ كُلُّ اُنْثٰى وَمَا تَغِيْضُ الْاَرْحَامُ وَمَا تَزْدَادُ ؕ وَكُلُّ شَىْءٍ عِنْدَهٗ بِمِقْدَارٍ‏(8)\nALLAAHO YA’LAMO MAA TAHMELO KULLO UNSAA WA MAA TAGHEEZU AL-AARHAAMU WA MAA TAZDAADU WA KULLO SHAY-IN I’NDAHU BEMEQDAARIN.\nGod knoweth what every female beareth, and that which the wombs fall short (of completion) and that in which they increase; And of every thing (there is) with Him a measure.\nعٰلِمُ الْغَيْبِ وَالشَّهَادَةِ الْكَبِيْرُ الْمُتَعَالِ‏(9)\nA’ALEMUL GHAYBE WASH SHAHAADATE AL-KABEERU AL-MUTAA’AALE.\nThe Knower of the unseen and the seen, the Great, the Most High.\nسَوَآءٌ مِّنْكُمْ مَّنْ اَسَرَّ الْقَوْلَ وَ مَنْ جَهَرَ بِهٖ وَمَنْ هُوَ مُسْتَخْفٍۢ بِالَّيْلِ وَسَارِبٌۢ بِالنَّهَارِ‏(10)\nSAWAAA-UN MINKUM MAN AASARRA QAWLA WA MAN JAHARA BEHI WA MAN HOWA MUSTAKHFIN BIL-LAYLE WASAAREBUN BEALNNAHAARE.\nAlike (unto him) among you is he who concealeth (his) speech or speaketh aloud, and he who hideth himself by night and (who) goeth forth by day.\nلَهٗ مُعَقِّبٰتٌ مِّنْۢ بَيْنِ يَدَيْهِ وَمِنْ خَلْفِهٖ يَحْفَظُوْنَهٗ مِنْ اَمْرِ اللّٰهِؕ اِنَّ اللّٰهَ لَا يُغَيِّرُ مَا بِقَوْمٍ حَتّٰى يُغَيِّرُوْا مَا بِاَنْفُسِهِمْؕ وَاِذَاۤ اَرَادَ اللّٰهُ بِقَوْمٍ سُوْۤءًا فَلَا مَرَدَّ لَهٗۚ وَمَا لَهُمْ مِّنْ دُوْنِهٖ مِنْ وَّالٍ‏(11)\nLAHU MUA’AQQEBAATUN MIN BAYNE YADAYHE WA MIN KHALFEH YAHFAZOONAH MIN AMRE LAAH INNAL LAAHA LAA YUGHAYRU MAA BE-QAWMIN HATTAA YUGHAYROOA MAA BEAANFUSEHEM WA EZAA ARAADA LAAHO BE-QAWMIN SOOAN FALAA MARADDA LAHU WA MAA LAHUM MIN DOONEHI MIN WWAALIN.\nFor him there are (angels) following one another, before him and behind him who guard him by God’s command; Verily God changeth not the condition of a people until they change what is in themselves; And when willeth God unto any people a punishment, there is no repelling of it for them, there is none besides Him a Protector.\nهُوَ الَّذِىْ يُرِيْكُمُ الْبَرْقَ خَوْفًا وَّطَمَعًا وَّيُنْشِئُ السَّحَابَ الثِّقَالَۚ‏(12)\nHOWA LAZEE AAYAATEHI YOREEKOMUL BARQA KHAWFANW WWAYUNSHEU AS-SAHAABA AS-SEQAALA.\nHe it is Who showeth you the lightning causing fear and hope and raiseth He the heavy (laden) clouds.\nوَيُسَبِّحُ الرَّعْدُ بِحَمْدِهٖ وَالْمَلٰۤئِكَةُ مِنْ خِيْفَتِهٖ ۚ وَيُرْسِلُ الصَّوَاعِقَ فَيُصِيْبُ بِهَا مَنْ يَّشَآءُ وَهُمْ يُجَادِلُوْنَ فِى اللّٰهۚ ِ وَهُوَ شَدِيْدُ الْمِحَالِؕ‏(13)\nWA YOSABBEHO AR-RAA’DU BEHAMDEH WAL MALAAEKATU MIN KHEEFATEH WA YURSELUR AS-SAWAAE’EQA FAYUSEEBU BEHAA MAN YASHAAA-O WA HUM YUJAADELOONA FIL AL-LAAH WA HOWA SHADEEDUL AL-MEHAALE.\nAnd glorifieth Him the thunder with His praise, and the angels too in awe for Him; and sendeth He the thunderbolts and smiteth He with them whom soever He willeth, and yet dispute they concerning God; while He is Mighty in prowess.\nلَهٗ دَعْوَةُ الْحَقِّؕ وَالَّذِيْنَ يَدْعُوْنَ مِنْ دُوْنِهٖ لَا يَسْتَجِيْبُوْنَ لَهُمْ بِشَىْءٍ اِلَّا كَبَاسِطِ كَفَّيْهِ اِلَى الْمَآءِ لِيَبْلُغَ فَاهُ وَمَا هُوَ بِبَالِغِهٖؕ وَمَا دُعَآءُ الْكٰفِرِيْنَ اِلَّا فِىْ ضَلٰلٍ‏(14)\nLAHU DAA’WATU HAQQ WAL LAZEENA YAD-O’ONA MIN DOONEHI LAA YASTAJEEBOONA LAHUM BE-SHAY-IM ILLAA KABAASETE KAFFAYHE ELAL AL-MAAE LE-HATTAA FAAHU WA MAA HOWA BEBAALEGHEH WA MAA DUA’AAU KAAFEREEN ILLAA FEE ZALAALIM.\nUnto Him (alone) is due the true prayer; and those unto whom they pray besides Him give not any answer unto them, but (they are) like one who stretcheth his two hands unto water that it may reach his mouth, but it will reach it not; and the prayer of the infidels doth nothing but goeth far astray.\nوَلِلّٰهِ يَسْجُدُ مَنْ فِى السَّمٰوٰتِ وَالْاَرْضِ طَوْعًا وَّكَرْهًا وَّظِلٰلُهُمْ بِالْغُدُوِّ وَالْاٰصَالِ ۩‏(15)\nLILLAAHE YASJUDU MAN FIL SAMAAWAATE WAL ARZE TEYAA WWAKARHAN WWAZELAALUHUM BIL-GHUDOO WAL AAASAALE.\nAnd unto God (alone) doth prostrate (in worship) whatever s in the heavens and the earth, willingly or by constraint, (so do) their shadows (also) at morn and eve.\nقُلْ مَنْ رَّبُّ السَّمٰوٰتِ وَالْاَرْضِؕ قُلِ اللّٰهُؕ قُلْ اَفَاتَّخَذْتُمْ مِّنْ دُوْنِهٖۤ اَوْلِيَآءَ لَا يَمْلِكُوْنَ لِاَنْفُسِهِمْ نَفْعًا وَّلَا ضَرًّاؕ قُلْ هَلْ يَسْتَوِى الْاَعْمٰى وَالْبَصِيْرُ ۙ اَمْ هَلْ تَسْتَوِى الظُّلُمٰتُ وَالنُّوْرُ ۚ اَمْ جَعَلُوْا لِلّٰهِ شُرَكَآءَ خَلَقُوْا كَخَلْقِهٖ فَتَشَابَهَ الْخَلْقُ عَلَيْهِمْؕ قُلِ اللّٰهُ خَالِقُ كُلِّ شَىْءٍ وَّهُوَ الْوَاحِدُ الْقَهَّارُ‏(16)\nQUL MAN RRABBU SAMAAWAATE WAL ARZ QOLIL LAAH QUL AAFAATTAKHAZTUM MIN DOONEHI AAWLEEAAAA LAA YAMLEKOONA LE-ANFOSEHIM BEKUM WA LAA ZARRAN QUL HAL YASTAWEAA A-A’MAA WAL BASEERU AM HAL LAA AZ-ZULUMAATU WAALNNOORU AM JAA’ALOOA LILLAAHE SHORA-KAAA-A KHALAQOOA KAKHALQEH FATASHAABAHA AL-KHALQU WA QOLIL LAAHO KHAALEQU KULLE SHAY-IN WA AL-WAAHEDU AL-QAHHAARU.\nSay thou (O’ Our Apostle Muhammad!) “Who is the Lord of the heavens and the earth?” Say: (thou) “God!” Say: What! “take ye then besides Him guardians who own neither any profit nor harm for themselves?” Say: (thou) “Are the blind and the seeing alike? or can darkness and light be equal?” or they have made unto God partners who have created (any) creation like unto His that what is created hath become confused unto them?” Say thou: “God (alone) is the Creator of all things, and He is (the Only) One, All-Dominant All-Mighty.\nاَنْزَلَ مِنَ السَّمَآءِ مَآءً فَسَالَتْ اَوْدِيَةٌۢ بِقَدَرِهَا فَاحْتَمَلَ السَّيْلُ زَبَدًا رَّابِيًا ؕ وَمِمَّا يُوْقِدُوْنَ عَلَيْهِ فِى النَّارِ ابْتِغَآءَ حِلْيَةٍ اَوْ مَتَاعٍ زَبَدٌ مِّثْلُهٗ ؕ كَذٰلِكَ يَضْرِبُ اللّٰهُ الْحَقَّ وَالْبَاطِلَ ؕ  فَاَمَّا الزَّبَدُ فَيَذْهَبُ جُفَآءً ۚ وَاَمَّا مَا يَنْفَعُ النَّاسَ فَيَمْكُثُ فِى الْاَرْضِؕ كَذٰلِكَ يَضْرِبُ اللّٰهُ الْاَمْثَالَؕ‏(17)\nANZALAL MENAL SAMAAA-E MAAA-AN FASAALAT AAWDEETUN BEQADAREHAA FAAHTAMALA AS-SAYLU ZABADAN RRAABEEA WA MIMMAA YOOQEDOONA A’LAYHE FIL NAAR TEGHAAA-A HELYATIN AW MATAAA’IN ZABADUN MMESLUH KAZAALEKA YAZREBU LAAHO HAQQA WAL BAATELA FA-AMMAA AZ-ZABADU FAYAZHABU JUFAAAN WA AMMAA MAA YANFAU’N NAASA FAYAMKUSU FIL ARZ KAZAALEKA YAZREBU LAAHO AL-AAMSAALA.\nHe sendeth down water from the heavens then the valleys flow according to their measure, and the torrent beareth along the swelling foam, (mounting to the surface); (Even so) and from that (the ore) what they melt in the fire for the sake of (making) ornaments or (the necessary) implements, arises a scum like it; Thus compareth God the truth and the falsehood; then as for the scum, it passeth away as a worthless thing; and as for that which profiteth the people, then it remaineth in the earth; Thus doth God set forth parables.\nلِلَّذِيْنَ اسْتَجَابُوْا لِرَبِّهِمُ الْحُسْنٰىؔؕ وَالَّذِيْنَ لَمْ يَسْتَجِيْبُوْا لَهٗ لَوْ اَنَّ لَهُمْ مَّا فِى الْاَرْضِ جَمِيْعًا وَّمِثْلَهٗ مَعَهٗ لَافْتَدَوْا بِهٖؕ اُولٰۤئِكَ لَهُمْ سُوْۤءُ الْحِسَابِ ۙ وَمَاْوٰٮهُمْ جَهَنَّمُؕ وَبِئْسَ الْمِهَادُ‏(18)\nLILLAZEENA ASTAJAABOOA LERABBEHEMU AL-HUSNAA WAL LAZEENA LAM YASTAJEEBOO LAHU LAW ANNAL LAHUM MAA FIL ARZE JAMEE-A’A WWAMESLAH MA-A’HU LAAFTADAWA BEH AOOLAAEKA LAHUM SOOU HESAAB WAMAAWAAHUM JAHANNAM WA WA BEASAL MEHAAD.\nFor those who respond to (the call of) their Lord is good; and (as for) those who respond not unto Him, even if they had all that is in the earth and the like thereof with it, they would certainly offer it for a ransom, (but in vain), for them shall be terrible reckoning, and their abode the Hell; and what a wretched resting place it will be!\nاَفَمَنْ يَّعْلَمُ اَنَّمَاۤ اُنْزِلَ اِلَيْكَ مِنْ رَّبِّكَ الْحَقُّ كَمَنْ هُوَ اَعْمٰىؕ اِنَّمَا يَتَذَكَّرُ اُولُوا الْاَلْبَابِۙ‏(19)\nAFAMAWN YYAA’LAMU ANNAMAA UNZELA ELAYKA MIN RABBEKA HAQQO KAMAM HOWA AAA’MAA INNAMAA YATAZAKKARU ULUL ULIL ALBAABE.\nIs then he who knoweth that what hath been sent down unto thee from thy Lord is truth, like unto him who is blind (void of knowledge)? will bear in mind only those possessed of understanding,\nالَّذِيْنَ يُوْفُوْنَ بِعَهْدِ اللّٰهِ وَلَا يَنْقُضُوْنَ الْمِيْثَاقَۙ‏(20)\nLAZEENA YOOFOONA BEA’AHDE LAAHE WA LAA YANQOZOONA AL-MEESAAQA.\nThose who fulfil the covenant of God (which) they have plight ed unto (themselves) and break not their pledge,\nوَالَّذِيْنَ يَصِلُوْنَ مَاۤ اَمَرَ اللّٰهُ بِهٖۤ اَنْ يُّوْصَلَ وَيَخْشَوْنَ رَبَّهُمْ وَ يَخَافُوْنَ سُوْۤءَ الْحِسَابِؕ‏(21)\nWAL LAZEENA YASELOONA MAA AMARAL LAAHO BEHI AN YOOSALA WA YAKHSHAWNA RABBAHUM WA YAKHAAFOONA SOOA AL-HESAABE.\nAnd those who join (establish) what God hath bidden to be joined (established) fear their Lord, and dread the terrible reckoning.\nوَالَّذِيْنَ صَبَرُوا ابْتِغَآءَ وَجْهِ رَبِّهِمْ وَاَقَامُوا الصَّلٰوةَ وَاَنْفَقُوْا مِمَّا رَزَقْنٰهُمْ سِرًّا وَّعَلَانِيَةً وَّيَدْرَءُوْنَ بِالْحَسَنَةِ السَّيِّئَةَ اُولٰۤئِكَ لَهُمْ عُقْبَى الدَّارِۙ‏(22)\nWAL LAZEENA SABAROOA TEGHAAA-A WAJHIL RABBEHIM WA AQAAMUS SALAATA WA ANFAQOO MIMMAA RAZAQNAAHUM SIRRAN WA A’LAANEYATAN WWAYADRAOONA BIL-HASANATE SAYYEATE AOOLAAEKA LAHUM U’UQBAA AD-DAARE.\nAnd those who are patient (amidst trials) seeking the countenance of their Lord, and establish prayer, and spend (benevolently) of what We have provided them with secretly and openly, and they turn away with good (even) evil for these is the (happy) attainment of the (Eternal) abode,\nجَنّٰتُ عَدْنٍ يَّدْخُلُوْنَهَا وَمَنْ صَلَحَ مِنْ اٰبَآئِهِمْ وَاَزْوَاجِهِمْ وَذُرِّيّٰتِهِمْ وَالْمَلٰٓئِكَةُ يَدْخُلُوْنَ عَلَيْهِمْ مِّنْ كُلِّ بَابٍۚ‏(23)\nJANNAATU A’ADNIN YYADKHULOONAHAA WA MAN SALAHA MIN AAABAAEHEM WA AZWAAJEHIM WAZURREETEHEM WAL MALAAA-EKATO YADKHOLOONA A’LAYHIM MIN KULLE BAABIN.\nThe garden of perpetual bliss which they will enter and also the righteous among their parents, their spouses, and their offspring; and the angels shall enter unto them from every portal.\nسَلٰمٌ عَلَيْكُمْ بِمَا صَبَرْتُمْ فَنِعْمَ عُقْبَى الدَّارِؕ‏(24)\nSALAAMUN A’LAYKUM BEMAA SABARTUM FA NE’MA U’UQBAA DAAR.\nPeace (be) unto you (Saying) for that ye persevered in patience! (and now) how excellent is the sequel of the eternal abode.\nوَالَّذِيْنَ يَنْقُضُوْنَ عَهْدَ اللّٰهِ مِنْۢ بَعْدِ مِيْثَاقِهٖ وَيَقْطَعُوْنَ مَاۤ اَمَرَ اللّٰهُ بِهٖۤ اَنْ يُّوْصَلَ وَيُفْسِدُوْنَ فِى الْاَرْضِۙ اُولٰۤئِكَ لَهُمُ اللَّعْنَةُ وَلَهُمْ سُوْۤءُ الدَّارِ‏(25)\nWAL LAZEENA YANQOZOONA A’HDAL LAAHE MIN BA’DE MEESAAQEH WA YAQTA-O’ONA MAA AMARAL LAAHO BEHI AN YOOSALA WA YUFSEDOONA FIL ARZE AOOLAAEKA LAHOMUL AL-LAA’NATU WA LAHUM SOOU AD-DAARE.\nAnd those who break the Covenant with God after it is pledged and cut asunder what God hath bidden to be joined and make mischief in the land, they, theirs shall be the curse and theirs shall be the terrible abode.\nاَللّٰهُ يَبْسُطُ الرِّزْقَ لِمَنْ يَّشَآءُ وَيَقْدِرُؕ وَفَرِحُوْا بِالْحَيٰوةِ الدُّنْيَا ؕ وَمَا الْحَيٰوةُ الدُّنْيَا فِى الْاٰخِرَةِ اِلَّا مَتَاعٌ‏(26)\nALLAAHO YABSOTUR RIZQA LEMAN-Y YASHAAA-O WA YAQDER WA FAREHOO BE-HAYAATID DUNYAA WA MAA HAYAATUD DUNYAA FIL AAKHERATE ILLAA LIL-MOTAALLAQAATE.\nGod amplifieth the sustenance for whomsoever He willeth and straiteneth it (similarly); and rejoice they in the life of this world; and nothing is the life of this world as heareafter but means.\nوَيَقُوْلُ الَّذِيْنَ كَفَرُوْا لَوْلَاۤ اُنْزِلَ عَلَيْهِ اٰيَةٌ مِّنْ رَّبِّهٖؕ قُلْ اِنَّ اللّٰهَ يُضِلُّ مَنْ يَّشَآءُ وَيَهْدِىْۤ اِلَيْهِ مَنْ اَنَابَ ۖ ۚ‏(27)\nWA YAQOOLO LAZEENA KAFAROO LAWLAA UNZELA A’LAYHE TAA-TEENAA MIN RABBEH QUL INNAL LAAHA YOZILLO MAN YASHAAA-O WA YAHDEE ELAYHE MAN AANAABA.\nAnd say those who disbelieve; “Why is not sent down unto him a sign from his Lord?” Say thou: “Verily God leaveth to stray whomsoever He willeth and guideth He unto Himself whomsoever turneth unto Him (seeking His way).\nاَلَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْا وَتَطْمَئِنُّ قُلُوْبُهُمْ بِذِكْرِ اللّٰهِ ؕ اَلَا بِذِكْرِ اللّٰهِ تَطْمَئِنُّ الْقُلُوْبُ ؕ‏(28)\nLAZEENA AAMANOO WATATMAENNU QULOOBUHUM BE-ELAA LAAHE ALAA BE-ELAA LAAHE TATMAENNU BALAGHATIL.\nAnd those who believe and their hearts are set at rest by God’s remembrance; Certainly! by God’s remembrance (only) are the hearts set at rest.\nاَلَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْا وَعَمِلُوا الصّٰلِحٰتِ طُوْبٰى لَهُمْ وَحُسْنُ مَاٰبٍ‏(29)\nLAZEENA AAMANOO WA A’MELUS SAALEHAATE TOOBAA LAHUM WAHUSNU MAABIN.\n(For) Those who believe and do good a great bliss shall be theirs and a beautiful place of return.\nكَذٰلِكَ اَرْسَلْنٰكَ فِىْۤ اُمَّةٍ قَدْ خَلَتْ مِنْ قَبْلِهَاۤ اُمَمٌ لِّتَتْلُوَا۟ عَلَيْهِمُ الَّذِىْۤ اَوْحَيْنَاۤ اِلَيْكَ وَ هُمْ يَكْفُرُوْنَ بِالرَّحْمٰنِؕ قُلْ هُوَ رَبِّىْ لَاۤ اِلٰهَ اِلَّا هُوَۚ عَلَيْهِ تَوَكَّلْتُ وَاِلَيْهِ مَتَابِ‏(30)\nKAZAALEKA ARSALNAAKA FEE UMMATIN QAD KHALAT MIN QABLEHAA OMAMUM LLETATLOOA A’LAYHEMUL LAZEE AAWHAYNAA ELAYKA WA HUM YAKFOROON BE-RAHMAAN QUL HOWA RABBEE LAA ELAAHA ILLAA HOWA A’LAYHE TAWAKKALTU WA ELAYHE MATAABE.\nThus did We send thee (O’ Our Apostle Muhammad!) among a people before whom other people have passed away, that thou mightest recite unto them (the Qur’an) what We have revealed unto thee while they deny the Beneficent (God). Say thou “He is my Lord, there is no god but He; on Him (only) do I rely, and unto Him is my return.\nوَلَوْ اَنَّ قُرْاٰنًا سُيِّرَتْ بِهِ الْجِبَالُ اَوْ قُطِّعَتْ بِهِ الْاَرْضُ اَوْ كُلِّمَ بِهِ الْمَوْتٰى ؕ بَلْ لِّلّٰهِ الْاَمْرُ جَمِيْعًا ؕ اَفَلَمْ يَايْئَسِ الَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْۤا اَنْ لَّوْ يَشَآءُ اللّٰهُ لَهَدَى النَّاسَ جَمِيْعًا ؕ وَلَا يَزَالُ الَّذِيْنَ كَفَرُوْا تُصِيْبُهُمْ بِمَا صَنَعُوْا قَارِعَةٌ اَوْ تَحُلُّ قَرِيْبًا مِّنْ دَارِهِمْ حَتّٰى يَاْتِىَ وَعْدُ اللّٰهِ ؕ اِنَّ اللّٰهَ لَا يُخْلِفُ الْمِيْعَادَ‏(31)\nWA LAW ANNAL QURAANAN SUYYERAT BEHIL JEBAALO AW QUTTEA’AT BEHIL ARZO AW KULLEMA BEHIL MAWTAA BAL LILLAAHE MIN JAMEE-A’A A-FALAM YAAYASE LAZEENA AAMANOO AN LAW YASHAAA LAAHO LAHADAA NAASA JAMEE-A’A WA LAA YAZAALU LAZEENA KAFAROO TUSEEBUHUM BEMAA SANAU’OOA QAAREA’ATUN AW TAHULLU QAREEBAA MIN DAAREHIM HATTAA HATTAA WAA’DU LAAHE INNAL LAAHA LAA YUKHLEFUL AL-MEEA’AADA.\nAnd (even) if there were a Qur’an by which the mountains were made to move, or the earth cloven asunder with it or the dead made to speak thereby; Nay! The command is wholly God’s; What! Have not those who believe yet known that if God willeth He would certainly guide all the people? And those who disbelieve, it will not cease to strike them for what they do, a torment, or it will alight close by their abodes, until cometh to pass the promise of God; Verily God faileth not in (His) promise.\nوَلَقَدِ اسْتُهْزِئَ بِرُسُلٍ مِّنْ قَبْلِكَ فَاَمْلَيْتُ لِلَّذِيْنَ كَفَرُوْا ثُمَّ اَخَذْتُهُمْ فَكَيْفَ كَانَ عِقَابِ‏(32)\nLAQADIS ASTUHZEA BERUSULIN MIN QABLEKA FAAMLAYTU LILLAZEENA KAFAROO SUMMA AAKHAZTUHUM FA-KAYFA KAANA E’EQAABE.\nAnd indeed were mocked at the apostles before thee, but I gave respite unto those who disbelieved, then I seized them; How then was My requital?\nاَفَمَنْ هُوَ قَآئِمٌ عَلٰى كُلِّ نَفْسٍۢ بِمَا كَسَبَتْۚ وَجَعَلُوْالِلّٰهِ شُرَكَآءَ ؕ قُلْ سَمُّوْهُمْؕ اَمْ تُنَبِّئُوْنَهٗ بِمَا لَا يَعْلَمُ فِى الْاَرْضِ اَمْ بِظَاهِرٍ مِّنَ الْقَوْلِؕ بَلْ زُيِّنَ لِلَّذِيْنَ كَفَرُوْا مَكْرُهُمْ وَصُدُّوْا عَنِ السَّبِيْلِؕ وَمَنْ يُّضْلِلِ اللّٰهُ فَمَا لَهٗ مِنْ هَادٍ‏(33)\nAFAMAWN HOWA QAAEMUN A’LAA KULLE NAFSIM BEMAA KASABAT WAJAA’ALOOALELLAAHE SHORA-KAAA-A QUL SAMMOOHUM AM TUNABEOONAH BEMAA LAA YA’LAMO FIL ARZE AM BEZAAHERIN MENAL AL-QAWLE BAL ZUYYENA LILLAZEENA KAFAROO MAKRUHUM WASUDDOOA A’NIL NIS SABEEL WA MAN YYUZLELE LAAHO FAMAA LAHU MIN HAADIN.\nWhat! Is He then who standeth (present) over every soul (and knoweth) what it doeth, (like the one otherwise)? And yet ascribe they partners unto God! Say thou (O’ Our Apostle Muhammad!) “Name them!” Is it that ye inform Him of what He knoweth not in the earth, Or is it (just) a show of words? Nay! But their contrivance are made to appear fairseeming unto those who disbelieve, and they kept back (thereby) from the (right) are path; and whom He (God) leaveth to stray, for him there shall be no guide.\nلَهُمْ عَذَابٌ فِى الْحَيٰوةِ الدُّنْيَا وَلَعَذَابُ الْاٰخِرَةِ اَشَقُّ ۚ وَمَا لَهُمْ مِّنَ اللّٰهِ مِنْ وَّاقٍ‏(34)\nLAHUM A’ZAABUN FIL HAYAATID DUNYAA LA-A’ZAABUL AAKHERATE AASHAQQU WA MAA LAHUM MENAL LAAHE MIN WWAAQIN.\nFor them is a torment in the life of this world, and surely the torment of hereafter is more grievous, and for them shall not be against God any protector.\nمَثَلُ الْجَنَّةِ الَّتِىْ وُعِدَ الْمُتَّقُوْنَ ؕ تَجْرِىْ مِنْ تَحْتِهَا الْاَنْهٰرُ ؕ اُكُلُهَا دَآئِمٌ وَّظِلُّهَا ؕ تِلْكَ عُقْبَى الَّذِيْنَ اتَّقَوْا ۖ  وَّعُقْبَى الْكٰفِرِيْنَ النَّارُ‏(35)\nMASALUL JANNAH LATEE WUE’EDA MUTTAQOON TAJREE MIN TAHTEHAL ANHAARO AUKULUHAA DAAEMUN WWAZELLUHAA TILKA U’UQBAA LAZEENA TAQAW WWAU’UQBAA KAAFEREEN TAMASSANAN.\nThe similitude of the garden (of bliss) promised unto the righteous; is that there flow beneath it rivers; there fruits are everlasting and its shade (too): This is the requital of those who guard (themselves) against evil, and the requital of the disbelievers is the (Hell) fire.\nوَالَّذِيْنَ اٰتَيْنٰهُمُ الْكِتٰبَ يَفْرَحُوْنَ بِمَاۤ اُنْزِلَ اِلَيْكَ وَمِنَ الْاَحْزَابِ مَنْ يُّنْكِرُ بَعْضَهٗؕ قُلْ اِنَّمَاۤ اُمِرْتُ اَنْ اَعْبُدَ اللّٰهَ وَلَاۤ اُشْرِكَ بِهٖؕ اِلَيْهِ اَدْعُوْا وَاِلَيْهِ مَاٰبِ‏(36)\nWAL LAZEENA AATAYNAAHOMUL KETAABA YAFRAHOONA BEMAA UNZELA ELAYKA WA MENAN AL-AAHZAABE MAN YYUNKERU BAA’ZAH QUL INNAMAA AN A-A’BODA AN HAAZEHIL BALDATIL LAAHA WA LAA AUSHREKA BEH ELAYHE AADU’OOA WA ELAYHE MAABE.\nAnd those whom We have given the Book rejoice in what hath been sent down unto thee, and of the clans are some who deny a part of it; Say thou: “Verily, I am only commanded that I should serve (only) God; and I associate not (aught) with Him; Unto Him (only) do I invite (ye all) and unto Him (only) is my return.\nوَكَذٰلِكَ اَنْزَلْنٰهُ حُكْمًا عَرَبِيًّا ؕ وَلَئِنِ اتَّبَعْتَ اَهْوَآءَهُمْ بَعْدَمَا جَآءَكَ مِنَ الْعِلْمِۙ مَا لَكَ مِنَ اللّٰهِ مِنْ وَّلِىٍّ وَّلَا وَاقٍ‏(37)\nWA KAZAALEKA ANZALNAAHO HUKMAWN A’RABIYYAL LA-ENIT TABA’TA AHWAAA-AHUM BA’DA MAA JAAA-AKA MENAL I’LME MAA LAKA MENAL LAAHE MIN WALIYYINW WA LAA WAAQIN.\nAnd thus have We sent it (the Qur’an) (a true) authority in (the) Arabic (language); and if followeth thou their (vain) desires after what hath come unto thee of the knowledge, there shall not be for thee besides God any guardian or a protector.\nوَلَقَدْ اَرْسَلْنَا رُسُلًا مِّنْ قَبْلِكَ وَ جَعَلْنَا لَهُمْ اَزْوَاجًا وَّذُرِّيَّةً  ؕ وَمَا كَانَ لِرَسُوْلٍ اَنْ يَّاْتِىَ بِاٰيَةٍ اِلَّا بِاِذْنِ اللّٰهِ ؕ لِكُلِّ اَجَلٍ كِتَابٌ‏(38)\nWA LAQAD ARSALNAA ROSOLAN MIN QABLEKA WA JA-A’LNAA LAHUM AZWAAJANW WWAZURREETAN WA MAA KAANA LE-RASOOLIN AN YAATEYA BE-AAYATIL ILLAA BE-IZNIL LAAHE LEKULLIM ELAA KETAABUN.\nAnd indeed We did send apostles before thee and gave We unto them wives and offspring! and it is not for an apostle to bring or (show) a sign (miracle) but by God’s permission; for every term there is a book prescribed.\nيَمْحُوْا اللّٰهُ مَا يَشَآءُ وَيُثْبِتُ ۖ ۚ وَعِنْدَهٗۤ اُمُّ الْكِتٰبِ‏(39)\nYAMHOOA LAAHO MAA YASHAAA WAYUSBETU WA I’NDAHU AUMMU KETAABE.\n( Of it) Effaceth out God whatever He pleaseth and confirmeth He (Similarly): and with Him is the Mother (Basic Source) of the Book.\nوَاِنْ مَّا نُرِيَنَّكَ بَعْضَ الَّذِىْ نَعِدُهُمْ اَوْ نَتَوَفَّيَنَّكَ فَاِنَّمَا عَلَيْكَ الْبَلٰغُ وَعَلَيْنَا الْحِسَابُ‏(40)\nWA MAA NUREENNAKA YAWM LAZEE NAE’EDUHUM AW NATAWAFFAYANNAKA FA-INNAMAA A’LAYKA BALAAGHUL WA A’LAYNAA AL-HESAABU.\nAnd We will either show thee a part of what We promised them or take unto ourselves thy soul (makes no difference), for verily on thee is (incumbent) only the delivery of the message and on Us the calling them to account.\nاَوَلَمْ يَرَوْا اَنَّا نَاْتِى الْاَرْضَ نَنْقُصُهَا مِنْ اَطْرَافِهَا ؕ وَاللّٰهُ يَحْكُمُ لَا مُعَقِّبَ لِحُكْمِهٖؕ وَهُوَ سَرِيْعُ الْحِسَابِ‏(41)\nAWALAM YARAW ANNAA NAATEAA ARZA NANQUSUHAA MIN AATRAAFEHAA WAL LAAHO YAHKOMO LAA MUA’AQQEBA LEHUKMEH WA HOWA SAREE-U’L HESAAB.\nSee they not that We come into their land and reduce its borders? Verily, God pronounceth a doom; there is no reverser for His command and He is swift in reckoning.\nوَقَدْ مَكَرَ الَّذِيْنَ مِنْ قَبْلِهِمْ فَلِلّٰهِ الْمَكْرُ جَمِيْعًاؕ يَعْلَمُ مَا تَكْسِبُ كُلُّ نَفْسٍؕ وَسَيَعْلَمُ الْكُفّٰرُ لِمَنْ عُقْبَى الدَّارِ‏(42)\nWA QAD MAKARA LAZEENA MIN QABLEHIM FALILLAAHE AL-MAKRU JAMEEA’AN YA’LAMO MAA TAKSEBU KULLO NAFSIN WASAYAA’LAMU AL-KUFFAARU LEMAN-Y U’UQBAA AD-DAARE.\nAnd indeed devised plots those before them but God’s is all planning; Knoweth He whatever every soul earneth, and soon will know the disbelievers for whom is the sequel of the eternal abode.\nوَيَقُوْلُ الَّذِيْنَ كَفَرُوْا لَسْتَ مُرْسَلًا ؕ قُلْ كَفٰى بِاللّٰهِ شَهِيْدًۢا بَيْنِىْ وَبَيْنَكُمْۙ وَمَنْ عِنْدَهٗ عِلْمُ الْكِتٰبِ‏(43)\nWA YAQOOLO LAZEENA KAFAROO LASTA MURSALAN QUL KAFAA BIL-LAAHE SHAHEEDAA BAYNEE WA BAYNAKUM WA MAN I’NDAHU I’LMUS KETAABE.\nAnd say those who disbelieve: “Thou art not an apostle (of God),” Say thou (O’ Our Apostle Muhammad!): “Sufficient is God a witness between me and you and he with whom is the knowledge of the Book.",
  "merits": "There are 43 verses in this Surah and it is ‘Makki’ though some Mufassireen (those who have written commentaries of the Holy Qur’an) say that the last verse of this Surah was revealed in Madinah. In fact, some even go as far as saying that the whole of this Surah is ‘Madani’ except for two verses.\nThe Holy Prophet (a.s.) has been quoted as saying that whoever recites this Surah will be made from among those who fulfil their promise to Allah (s.w.t.) and they will be given reward which is ten times the number of sins they have committed.\nIt is narrated that Imam Ja’far al-Sadiq (a.s.) has said that if a believer recites this Surah often, he will be taken to Jannah without having to give the long and detailed accounts for his deeds on Earth. He will also be allowed to intercede on behalf of his relatives and friends.\nIf this Surah is written at night, after the time for Isha prayers, under a candle’s light, and then hung outside the door of a tyrant ruler’s palace, then the ruler will perish and so will his control over the people. His army and his supporters will betray him and nobody will listen to him."
